<%# locals: (message:, folder:, reply_form: nil, notice: nil, streams: []) %>
<%#
  The conversation pane: the selected thread beside the list from lg up, the
  whole page below it. The aside is what review_pane_controller watches; the
  messages-pane frame inside it is what a row's link loads (MessagesConcern#show
  answers that request with this partial alone). The frame targets _top, and the
  Mark Read, Archive and reply forms inside it keep their own frames, so they
  submit as they did on the thread page.

  The frame is rendered disabled. Turbo hands a link to a frame only while the
  frame is enabled, so until review_pane_controller enables it from lg up -- or
  with no script at all -- a row's link is an ordinary visit to the thread page.

  With nothing selected -- the index -- the pane is hidden below lg, where the
  list is the whole page. `notice` says why a row's thread could not be shown
  (MessagesConcern#refuse_message). `streams` are turbo-streams that ride inside
  the frame and run as it renders: what reading the thread changed outside the
  pane (MessagesConcern#read_state_streams).
%>
<%# review-pane (components/review-pane.css) caps the height from lg up so a long thread scrolls inside;
    scroll-my-4 keeps a gap when review_pane_controller brings it on screen from under the list. %>
<aside class="<%= class_names("review-pane box box-default p-4 scroll-my-4 lg:flex-1 lg:min-w-0 lg:sticky lg:top-4 lg:self-start",
                              "hidden lg:block": message.nil?) %>"
       aria-label="Conversation" data-review-pane-target="pane">
  <%= turbo_frame_tag "messages-pane", target: "_top", disabled: true, data: { turbo_action: "advance" } do %>
    <% if message %>
      <%= render partial: "common/messages/messages_panel", locals: { message:, folder:, reply_form: } %>
    <% else %>
      <% if notice %>
        <%= ui_callout_box :warning, role: "status" do %><%= notice %><% end %>
      <% end %>
      <%= ui_empty_state "Select a conversation to read it here.", icon: "hand-pointer", icon_type: :solid %>
    <% end %>
    <%= safe_join(streams) %>
  <% end %>
</aside>
